{"id": "20563573", "revid": "27823944", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki?curid=20563573", "title": "Woodlawn (St. Marys, Maryland)", "text": "Woodlawn is a historic home located at St. Mary's City, St. Mary's County, Maryland, United States. It is a Federal-style, two-story, five-bay frame house with brick ends, which is two rooms deep and has a gable roof. Each brick end contains a large double exterior chimney. The house is a large and fully developed Federal period house exhibiting one of the most important characteristics of Southern Maryland's 18th-century architecture: brick ends with frame facades. It is operated as a bed and breakfast.\nWoodlawn was listed on the National Register of Historic Places in 1980."}
{"id": "20563574", "revid": "20480869", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki?curid=20563574", "title": "Wyatt, Tarrant &amp; Combs", "text": "Wyatt, Tarrant &amp; Combs LLP is an American regional law firm with its largest office in Louisville, Kentucky. The firm traces its roots back more than 200 years to 1812, when Alexander Scott Bullitt opened his law practice. Wyatt has changed significantly since those frontier days and is now a full-service regional law firm with offices in Louisville and Lexington, Kentucky; New Albany, Indiana; and Memphis and Nashville, Tennessee. "}
