{"id": "20563607", "revid": "43579", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki?curid=20563607", "title": "Geranium dalmaticum", "text": "Geranium dalmaticum, commonly called Dalmatian cranesbill, is a species of hardy flowering herbaceous perennial plant in the genus \"Geranium\" of the family Geraniaceae. It is native to the Pelje\u0161ac peninsula of Dalmatia on the west coast of Croatia. Growing to only tall by up to broad, it is cultivated as a garden subject in temperate regions for its low mound of aromatic leaves and soft mauve colored flowers. The palmately lobed glossy green leaves are tinted red in the Autumn. It has gained the Royal Horticultural Society's Award of Garden Merit."}
