{"id": "20565014", "revid": "277086", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki?curid=20565014", "title": "David Madden (politician)", "text": "David John Madden (1880 \u2013 31 July 1955) was an Irish Fine Gael politician, farmer and auctioneer. He was elected to Seanad \u00c9ireann in April 1938 by the Industrial and Commercial Panel. He was re-elected to the Seanad in July 1938, 1943 and 1944.\nHe was elected to D\u00e1il \u00c9ireann as a Fine Gael Teachta D\u00e1la (TD) for the Limerick West constituency at the 1948 general election. He was re-elected at the 1951 and 1954 general elections. He died in office in 1955 during the 15th D\u00e1il; the resulting by-election, held on 13 December 1955, was won by Michael Colbert of Fianna F\u00e1il."}
