{"id": "20565671", "revid": "9784415", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki?curid=20565671", "title": "Clinopodium acinos", "text": "Clinopodium acinos, many synonyms including Acinos arvensis, known commonly as basil thyme and spring savory, is a species of flowering plant in the family Lamiaceae.\nIt is a perennial that usually grows about high and spreads . It prefers to grow in strong sunlight. The scent is faintly reminiscent of thyme, giving it one of its common names.\n\"Clinopodium acinos\" is recorded as a food plant for the larva of the moth \"Coleophora tricolor\"."}
