{"id": "20566213", "revid": "15881234", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki?curid=20566213", "title": "Hart's Woods", "text": "Hart's Woods is a small forest located in Perinton, New York. It contains a pristine stand of beech-maple forest, which covered 47% of Perinton prior to settlement. This type of forest with two dominant tree species thrives in areas of glacial till. The site was declared a National Natural Landmark in June 1972.\nHart's Woods is open to the public for hiking on its trail system. It is operated by the Town of Perinton Recreation and Parks Department."}
