{"id": "20566685", "revid": "2068487", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki?curid=20566685", "title": "More Twisted Christmas", "text": "More Twisted Christmas (alternately titled \"Bob Rivers Presents More Twisted Christmas\") is the third Christmas album by Bob Rivers &amp; Twisted Radio, released in 1997. Whereas the first two albums in the \"Twisted Christmas\" series featured some original songs, spoken word comedy and instrumentals, all of the songs on this album are direct parodies, either Christmas-themed parodies of popular songs or parodies of Christmas songs.\nThe album was in the top 20 of Billboard's Top Heatseekers album charts in December 1997."}
{"id": "20566688", "revid": "3617193", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki?curid=20566688", "title": "Geranium himalayense", "text": "Geranium himalayense (common names Himalayan crane's-bill or lilac cranesbill) is a species of hardy flowering herbaceous perennial plant in the genus \"Geranium\", family Geraniaceae. It is native to West Himalaya, Afghanistan, Kyrgyzstan, Nepal, Pakistan, Tajikistan, Tibet, and Uzbekistan.\nIt has a sprawling habit, violet-blue flowers and deeply cut palmate foliage. It grows in alpine and subalpine meadows."}
