{"id": "20567856", "revid": "9784415", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki?curid=20567856", "title": "John Carew (Irish politician)", "text": "John Carew (5 May 1901 \u2013 12 July 1968) was an Irish Fine Gael politician. He was elected to D\u00e1il \u00c9ireann as a Fine Gael Teachta D\u00e1la (TD) for the Limerick East constituency at the 1952 by-election caused by the death of Daniel Bourke of Fianna F\u00e1il. He was re-elected at the 1954 and 1957 general elections but lost his seat at the 1961 general election.\nHe was a member of Limerick City Council from 1942 until his death in 1968, and was Mayor of Limerick from 1953 to 1954 and 1959 to 1960."}
