{"id": "20567935", "revid": "9784415", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki?curid=20567935", "title": "Daniel Bourke", "text": "Daniel Bourke (1886 \u2013 13 April 1952) was an Irish Fianna F\u00e1il politician. A wagon builder before entering politics, he was first elected to D\u00e1il \u00c9ireann as a Fianna F\u00e1il Teachta D\u00e1la (TD) at the September 1927 general election for the Limerick constituency. He was re-elected at every subsequent general election up to 1951, and from 1948 for the Limerick East constituency. He died in 1952 during the 14th D\u00e1il, a by-election was held on 26 June 1952 which was won by John Carew of Fine Gael.\nHe was Mayor of Limerick from 1936 until 1941."}
